<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Vigraharaja II</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">10th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Vigraharaja II was a king of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chauhan">Chahamanas</a> of Shakambhari in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajasthan">Rajasthan</a> in the late 10th century. Breaking free of the declining Gurjara-Pratiharas, he asserted the dynasty's independence, and he is recorded as defeating <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mularaja">Mularaja</a>, founder of the Chaulukya kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gujarat">Gujarat</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/harsha">Harsha</a> stone inscription of 973, from his reign, is a key source for the early Chahamanas.</p></div>
